SNOW WHITE — an 80s Cel Anime short (1920×1080, 24 fps)

Story: "Snow White" (Sneewittchen), Brothers Grimm, 1812 — public domain.
  Retelling, script and Vietnamese subtitles written for this film.
  Disney-specific inventions (the dwarfs' names and designs) are not used.
Animation, backgrounds, score and sound design: generated by code in
  this folder (Canvas 2D, WebGL, numpy). No stock art, no samples.
Voice: Kokoro TTS (Apache 2.0), voice bf_emma (English, narration).
Fonts (SIL Open Font License 1.1, licence texts in fonts/):
  Dela Gothic One (artakana), Kanit (Cadson Demak),
  Barlow Semi Condensed (Jeremy Tribby).
Production tool: the lemo-opuscar library (MIT) — a tool, not content;
  the film carries no library credit or watermark.
